A merge joins two histories, a rebase

12
00:00:54,513 --> 00:00:59,033
and a cherry-pick copy commits, and a
revert adds a commit that undoes one.

13
00:00:59,073 --> 00:01:03,897
They looked like four topics. They are
one mechanism, the three-way merge, which

14
00:01:03,937 --> 00:01:08,761
combines two versions against a common
base, used with four different choices of

15
00:01:08,801 --> 00:01:12,348
inputs, plus one question about
history: private or shared.

16
00:01:14,188 --> 00:01:15,766
Here's what you'll walk away with.

17
