86
00:06:08,114 --> 00:06:09,762
Five mistakes to watch for.

87
00:06:10,102 --> 00:06:13,829
Taking --ours in a stopped
rebase to keep your own change.

88
00:06:13,869 --> 00:06:19,091
Root cause: ours is HEAD, and in a rebase
HEAD is the side you are rebasing onto.

89
00:06:19,431 --> 00:06:22,473
Starting to resolve before
identifying the operation.

90
00:06:22,513 --> 00:06:27,124
Root cause: the exits and the meaning of
the stages depend on whether a merge, a

91
00:06:27,164 --> 00:06:29,973
rebase, a cherry-pick or
a revert is in progress.

92
00:06:30,313 --> 00:06:34,680
Reaching a correct end state with
git reset --hard or a forced push.

93
00:06:34,720 --> 00:06:39,605
Root cause: the safety of the path is
scored separately, and a safer command

94
00:06:39,645 --> 00:06:40,123
existed.

95
00:06:40,463 --> 00:06:44,988
Reading A..B the same way for git log
and git diff in a prediction item.

96
00:06:45,028 --> 00:06:50,250
Root cause: log selects commits by reachability;
diff compares two trees, and three

97
00:06:50,290 --> 00:06:52,215
dots there mean the merge base.

98
00:06:52,555 --> 00:06:55,961
Choosing an undo without asking
whether the commits are shared.

99
00:06:56,001 --> 00:07:00,337
Root cause: the decision tree branches on
publication before it names a command.

100
00:07:02,177 --> 00:07:06,775
Now, out of the lab. What this gate
examines is the on-call situation: you are

101
00:07:06,815 --> 00:07:11,710
